  "body": "Three published lesson passages implied guaranteed behavior or a rigorous learning process. Replace those implications with bounded descriptions of the exercise while preserving the valuation arithmetic and stored course records. Also correct the double-bottom explanation: a higher RSI reading does not establish smaller absolute price declines, because RSI compares average gains with average losses.\n\nValidation: complete local Cloudflare build including course HTML/bootstrap, idempotence, later-owner-edit preservation and editorial regressions passed. Added an independent RSI counterexample (25 to 32 while average losses rise from 3 to 6). Fidelity formula source and pre-edit evidence are recorded in continuation-2026-11-22/DEFECT-EVENTS.jsonl. Protected CI and native production verification remain required before closure. Ad serving remains disabled; no AdSense submission or account/CMP changes. Continues #430; does not close the audit or certify readiness.",
